  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 15.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#2f5496"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 207.62pt, "Abstract ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 223.94pt, "Nucleate pool boiling is known for its exceptional heat transfer coefficients, with the use of cavities ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 238.46pt, "further improving bubble nucleation and heat transfer rate. To promote this heat transfer ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 252.86pt, "enhancement technique, a thorough understanding of the influence of cavity geometry on single ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 267.41pt, "bubble dynamics is required. The influence of depth and radius of cylindrical and conical cavities on ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 281.93pt, "the bubble dynamics of nucleate pool boiling of R1234yf were numerically investigated. The cavity ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 296.45pt, "radius was varied between 50 μm and 400 μm and the cavity depth between 100 μm and 1000 μm at ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 310.85pt, "a fixed heat flux of 28 kW/m")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(198.29pt, 306.89pt, "2")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(201.77pt, 310.85pt, ". It was found that the maximum equivalent diameter prior to departure ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 325.37pt, "was constant for cavities with radii smaller than 120 μm, while it increased linearly when increasing ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 339.89pt, "the cavity radius further. Cylindrical cavities exhibited high stability regardless of cavity radius or depth ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 354.41pt, "whereas conical cavities showed a decrease in vapour retention with increasing cavity angle. During ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 368.81pt, "the necking phase, the bubble interface became pinned at the cavity edge, depending on conical cavity ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 383.33pt, "angle, implying that smaller radii allowed for enhanced surface rewetting. Conical cavities could be ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 397.85pt, "considered as cylindrical cavities when the cavity angle was less than a quarter of the interface contact ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 412.37pt, "angle. When translating the single cavity findings to cavity array design, cylindrical cavities were ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 426.77pt, "recommended as they allowed for stable bubble behaviour. For increased nucleation zones and ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 441.31pt, "rewetting, a sub-critical radius was recommended. Wider cavities were recommended for high ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 455.83pt, "superheat conditions as larger bubbles could enhance bubble growth. ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 478.27pt, "Keywords: Nucleate Pool Boiling, Cavity Geometry, Bubble Dynamics, Volume of Fluid, Numerical ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 492.79pt, "Modelling ")
]

