  #line-at(100.82pt, 240.14pt, "Boundary Conditions and Initial Conditions ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 255.26pt, "A schematic of the calculation domain showing the boundary conditions is given in Figure 2. The ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 269.81pt, "domain was axisymmetric, implying the front and back surfaces were treated as symmetry boundary ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 284.21pt, "conditions, while the left-hand surface was the axis. Separate solid and fluid domains allowed for the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 298.73pt, "modelling of conjugate heat transfer. The bottom surface was heated with a constant heat flux while a ")
