  #line-at(72.024pt, 544.03pt, "For the cylindrical cavities, the meshing was straightforward, using a structured hex-mesh (Figure 3(a)) ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 558.43pt, "and only relying on unstructured mesh cells at the interfaces between the zones of different cell sizes. ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 572.95pt, "For the conical cavities, the snappyHexMesh utility of OpenFOAM was used to capture the diagonal ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 587.47pt, "line of the cavity surface, introducing triangular cells along this line (Figure 3(b)). For the conical ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 601.99pt, "cavities, a sharp point at the apex of the cone created highly skewed, non-orthogonal cells which ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 616.39pt, "resulted in numerical instability.  It was considered reasonable to flatten this apex as many fabrication ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 630.94pt, "techniques would fail at rendering a perfectly pointed conical cavity. ")
]

// arXiv source page 13
#original-page(595.32pt, 841.92pt, (image("graphics/page-13.png", width: 451.5pt), 72pt, 72pt))[
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(512.26pt, 790.176pt, "13 ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 9pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(81.144pt, 259.22pt, "Figure 3: Sample images contrasting the structure of the mesh generated for (a) cylindrical cavity and (b) conical cavity. ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 282.05pt, "A mesh independence study was performed investigating the impact of cell size on the departure ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 296.57pt, "dynamics. As the mesh was divided into four zones, it allowed for variable refinement, with fine cells ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 310.97pt, "in the region of bubble growth and progressively coarser cells further away. This was done to reduce ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 325.49pt, "the total cell count and obtain a faster solution time. The coarsest mesh size was 50 μm which was ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 340.01pt, "implemented throughout the calculation domain. For smaller cell sizes, zone A (Figure 2), had a cell ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 354.53pt, "size of 40 μm, which was then halved to 20 μm in zone B, 10 μm in zone C, and finally 5 μm in zone D. ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 368.93pt, "Since the cavity size considered in the mesh independence study had a radius of 100 μm, 40 μm cells ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 383.45pt, "could not accurately capture the cavity’s geometry resulting in only cell sizes of 5 μm, 10 μm, 20 μm ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 397.97pt, "and 50 μm having been tested.  ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 420.41pt, "Three metrics were used to compare the results: (1) equivalent bubble diameter at departure (")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(489.94pt, 420.41pt, "D")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(496.66pt, 421.37pt, "eq, dep")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(517.18pt, 420.41pt, "), ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 434.93pt, "(2) bubble growth time (")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(184.94pt, 434.93pt, "t")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(188.69pt, 435.89pt, "dep")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(199.13pt, 434.93pt, "), and (3) equivalent diameter of the remaining vapour attached to the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 449.47pt, "surface after departure (")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(180.14pt, 449.47pt, "D")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(187.01pt, 450.43pt, "rem")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(198.17pt, 449.47pt, "). Table III summarises the results of the mesh independence study, taking ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 463.99pt, "the finest (5 μm) mesh as a reference. Figure 4 visualises these results to show the difference in growth ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 478.39pt, "rates. As the results from the 10 μm mesh closely agreed with those of the 5 μm mesh, with all ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 492.91pt, "departure metrics being within 5% for the two meshes, it was concluded that acceptable mesh ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 507.43pt, "independence was achieved using a 10 μm cell size. This also corresponded well with cell sizes used in ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 521.95pt, "similar studies in literature [19, 24, 34]. ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 9pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
