  #line-at(76.464pt, 364.49pt, "Figure 4: Bubble growth curves showing the results of the mesh independence study for minimum cell sizes of 5 μm (blue), ")
  #line-at(86.664pt, 375.41pt, "10 μm (green), 20 μm (red), 50 μm (orange). Also, shown is how the difference in growth time and remaining bubble ")
  #line-at(250.85pt, 386.45pt, "diameter were measured. ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 12.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#2f5496"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 411.29pt, "2.5")
  #line-at(100.82pt, 411.29pt, "Validation of the Numerical Model ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 426.41pt, "The experimental results of Li et al. [36], using R1234yf with an input heat flux of 28 kW/m")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(469.3pt, 422.45pt, "2")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(472.78pt, 426.41pt, ", were used ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 440.83pt, "for the validation. To achieve single bubble nucleation, Li et al. [36] made use of a cylindrical cavity ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 455.35pt, "with a depth of 500 μm and a radius of 100 μm, drilled into the centre of the top surface of a 5 mm-")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 469.87pt, "diameter copper rod.  ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 492.31pt, "The initial single-phase simulations had an arbitrarily selected runtime of 0.24 s, and various initial ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 506.83pt, "solid superheats were considered. Thereafter, the results from the two-phase simulations were ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 521.35pt, "compared with the validation case and the initial conditions were fine-tuned to achieve agreement ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 535.87pt, "with the experimental data. The validation results of numerical model and initial conditions are ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 550.27pt, "summarised in Table IV and visualised in Figure 5. The experimental data [36] and ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(444.22pt, 550.27pt, "D")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(451.06pt, 551.23pt, "rem")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(462.34pt, 550.27pt, " values of the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 564.79pt, "numerical simulations show an initial bubble diameter of 0.31 mm due to a small portion of vapour ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 579.31pt, "remaining attached to the cavity after the previous bubble departure. Due to limits in computational ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 593.83pt, "power and the possibility of complete vapour detachment from certain cavities, the numerical results ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 608.23pt, "presented in this study encompass only the first bubble’s lifecycle. This creates a discrepancy in the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 622.78pt, "initial bubble size of the experimental and numerical results. As indicated in Figure 5, the discrepancy ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 637.3pt, "in the initial bubble size is overcome by considering numerical results after the point that they reached ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 651.82pt, "the initial experimental bubble size. The equivalent diameter at departure and the bubble remaining ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 666.22pt, "after departure were in close agreement with the experimental results (within 4%) regardless of the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 680.74pt, "initial temperature of the solid. The bubble size after departure was compared with the first datum of ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 695.26pt, "the experimental results, as this would have been recorded after the departure of the previous bubble. ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 709.78pt, "The only metric significantly influenced by the initial temperature of the solid was the bubble growth ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 724.18pt, "time. An initial surface superheat of 4.85 K was shown to yield the best overall results with all ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 738.7pt, "departure metrics being within 2% of the experimental results. ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 9pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(130.7pt, 759.456pt, "Table IV: Results of validation study using different initial temperatures for the solid domain. ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 11.064pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(395.47pt, 259.1pt, "∆𝐷")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 8.064pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(409.15pt, 261.38pt, "𝑟𝑒𝑚")
