  #line-at(72.024pt, 125.9pt, "wide-angle conical cavities. ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 148.46pt, "The red curves from Figure 13(a) and blue curves from Figure 13(b) sometimes deviated from this ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 162.86pt, "general trend, which indicated that deeper cavities can also increase the bubble departure time. These ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 177.38pt, "exceptions were found to be caused by the rapid bubble growth within the cavity disrupting the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 191.9pt, "thermal boundary layer (as shown in Figure 14(c)), resulting in a decreased growth rate after ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 206.42pt, "emergence from the cavity. This is also visible from the gradient of the bubble growth curve being ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 220.82pt, "slightly less for the specific cases.  ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 243.38pt, "When comparing the predicted and numerical results, the agreement is seen to vary depending on the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 257.9pt, "cavity geometry. Across all cavities the correlation of Sakashita [43] performed the best with an ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 272.33pt, "average deviation of 11.3% for cylindrical cavities and 15.53% for conical cavities. The correlation of ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 286.85pt, "Cole and Shulman [44] had the largest average deviations of 21.9% and 34.5% for cylindrical and ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 301.37pt, "conical cavities, respectively. Good agreement between the correlations and numerical results were ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 315.89pt, "observed in the supercritical radius range (a radius larger than 120 μm) and moderate depth (500 to ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 330.29pt, "1000 μm). In the case of conical cavities, significant deviations were observed for large cavity angles. ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 344.81pt, "Although some deviations as low as 0.3% existed for some cavities, the large disparity in the deviations ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 359.33pt, "indicated that the correlations were not suitable for the use of cavity array boiling surfaces. For such ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 373.85pt, "needs, the correlations need to account for the cavity geometry, which remains as an interesting ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 388.25pt, "avenue for future work. ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 9pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#44546a"))
