  #line-at(72.024pt, 417.17pt, "in departure frequency increased for the shallow cavity. The deeper cavity showed lower deviation ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 431.69pt, "causing a growing disparity in departure frequency from the two cavities. ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 454.15pt, "Therefore, for the design of low superheat systems, the cylindrical cavity depth may be largely ignored. ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 468.67pt, "For high superheat systems, deeper cavities may offer higher stability and more regular bubble ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 483.19pt, "departure. As will be shown in Section 3.3, the cavity angle of conical cavities affects the departure ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 497.71pt, "time and cavity stability. Therefore, more attention should be given to the cavity depth when designing ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 512.11pt, "a system with conical cavities since the cavity depth and cavity angle are related. ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 12.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#2f5496"))
